          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Dumas's Writing Style</strong><br>\nDumas's novels are known for their fast-paced narratives, adventure, and historical settings. He collaborated with other writers to produce his vast array of works, which also included plays and travel books.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Historical Novels</strong><br>\nDumas wrote extensively in the historical novel genre. His works, often based on French history, combined real historical events and figures with fictitious characters, creating a blend that educated and entertained his readers.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Personal Struggles</strong><br>\nDespite his success, Dumas faced racism due to his African ancestry, stemming from his paternal grandmother who was a slave in Haiti. He also struggled financially due to extravagant spending and the challenge of supporting his illegitimate children.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
