            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Political Engagement</strong><br>\nDumas was politically active, participating in the Revolution of 1830 which brought Louis-Philippe to the throne. His writings sometimes reflect his political ideals, advocating for democracy and freedom.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Travel and Late Career</strong><br>\nLater in life, Dumas spent several years traveling, especially in Italy, where he supported the unification efforts. His travel experiences enriched his later works with diverse settings and international perspectives.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Death</strong><br>\nAlexandre Dumas died in 1870, leaving behind a legacy as one of France's most widely read authors. His works have been translated into numerous languages, and his stories have been adapted into over 200 films.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
